To ensure effective ventilation, it is important to avoid placing obstructions such as furniture or heavy curtains in front of air vents and doors. Overcrowding in a room should also be avoided as it can restrict airflow. Additionally, using excessive insulation or sealing too tightly can prevent proper air circulation.

