This context outlines a step-by-step process for performing rescue breathing during a cardiac arrest situation. First, ensure the airway is open with a head tilt-chin lift, then give a breath over 1 second while observing if the chest rises. If the chest doesn't rise, repeat the head tilt-chin lift and try another breath. If the second breath also fails to go in, start chest compressions immediately. This procedure helps maintain oxygen supply to vital organs while awaiting professional medical assistance.
